# Git conventions

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) for every commit message and pull request title.

Format: `type(scope): description`

- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`
- Subject is lowercase, imperative, no trailing period
- `feat` bumps minor, `fix`/`perf` bump patch, `BREAKING CHANGE` or `type!:` bumps major
- `chore`/`ci`/`docs` do not create a release by themselves

Pull requests use `.github/pull_request_template.md`. After merge to `main`, semantic-release tags `vX.Y.Z` and publishes a GitHub Release. Do not hand-edit version tags unless the user asks.
